 5038|       |			-DHonor_FLT_ROUNDS, modes 4 and 5 behave the same
 5039|       |			as modes 2 and 3 when FLT_ROUNDS != 1.
 5040|       |		6-9 ==> Debugging modes similar to mode - 4:  don't try
 5041|       |			fast floating-point estimate (if applicable).
 5042|       |
 5043|       |		Values of mode other than 0-9 are treated as mode 0.
 5044|       |
 5045|       |	When not NULL, buf is an output buffer of length blen, which must
 5046|       |	be large enough to accommodate suppressed trailing zeros and a trailing
 5047|       |	null byte.  If blen is too small, rv = NULL is returned, in which case
 5048|       |	if rve is not NULL, a subsequent call with blen >= (*rve - rv) + 1
 5049|       |	should succeed in returning buf.
 5050|       |
 5051|       |	When buf is NULL, sufficient space is allocated for the return value,
 5052|       |	which, when done using, the caller should pass to freedtoa().
